<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gukhak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">682</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gukhak was the national Confucian academy of Silla, founded in 682 under King Sinmun to train young aristocrats for government service. Students studied the Confucian classics such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/analects">Analects</a> and the Classic of Filial Piety. It reflected Unified Silla's adoption of Tang Chinese models of government and learning.</p></div>
